Knnn wrote:
> What about statistics from devnull?  You have a lot more
> "serial ascenders", but surely you also have lots of less
> qualified players.  Besides, doesn't the time limit of the
> tourney make people play "more seriously" - giving you
> a better grounded set of statistics?

The problem with using devnull statistics is twofold.

One -- the optional Challenges.  Someone attempting to complete last
year's challenge has a significant disadvantage in the early game, which
affects some classes' play more than others.  Someone adhering to this
year's challenge could have suffered a large number of unavoidable deaths.

Two -- Conducts, score, and "most unique deaths" are all valid
objectives in and of themselves in the tournament.  Someone attempting
pacifist conduct, for example, is going to die a lot more frequently
than people just snowplowing through to ascend.  Someone attempting
most-unique-deaths, well, that speaks for itself.

Neither is trivial to filter out from just the logfile data; some aren't
trivial to filter out short of "watching the person play".  So devnull
actually becomes a very ineffective data source.

